const faq = [
  ["Can foreigners buy property in Ras Al Khaimah?", "Yes, in the designated freehold areas. Ras Al Khaimah Municipality lists them as Al Hamra Village, Mina Al Arab, Al Marjan Island, RAK Central, Julphar Towers, Al Maareedh (plots) and the upcoming Beach District. UAE and GCC nationals can buy anywhere in the Emirate."],
  ["What does freehold mean in Ras Al Khaimah?", "Full ownership in your own name, recorded on a title deed. Before you pay a deposit, confirm that the exact plot or building sits inside a freehold area."],
  ["Can foreigners buy property in Downtown RAK?", "Only in designated projects. In <a class=\"ulink\" href=\"/areas#downtown-rak\">Downtown RAK</a>, freehold is limited to designated projects such as Julphar Towers and RAK Central."],
  ["Do I need to live in the UAE to buy property in Ras Al Khaimah?", "Not necessarily. Foreign nationals can buy freehold whether they are UAE residents or live overseas. We run video viewings for buyers abroad, and a power of attorney can be used if someone acts for you at the transfer."],
  ["Can foreigners buy off-plan property in Ras Al Khaimah?", "Yes. <a class=\"ulink\" href=\"/al-marjan-island\">Al Marjan Island</a> is freehold, so foreign buyers can own off-plan units there outright, the same as ready homes. Our current book carries <a class=\"ulink\" href=\"/off-plan#off-plan-projects-list\">nine off-plan launches on the island</a>."],
  ["What government fees do foreigners pay when buying in Ras Al Khaimah?", "The buyer pays a registration fee of 2% of the market value to RAK Municipality, plus AED 200 for plan issuance and AED 200 for the title deed. If you use a mortgage, its registration costs 0.1% of the loan. Agency commission and developer charges are separate."],
  ["Is there tax on property in the UAE?", "There is no income tax or capital gains tax on property in the UAE. The registration fees still apply when you buy."],
  ["How do foreigners buy property in Ras Al Khaimah?", "Set your budget and goal, shortlist an area, view the property, reserve and sign (an MOU for a resale or the developer’s SPA for off-plan), get the developer’s NOC, then transfer and register at RAK Municipality, pay the registration fee and receive the title deed."],
  ["Does buying property in Ras Al Khaimah give me a Golden Visa?", "It can. Property worth AED 2M or more can qualify you for a UAE Golden Visa, subject to the federal ICP rules at the time you apply. Official pages differ on whether the property route gives 5 or 10 years, so confirm the term with ICP or your RAK channel. RFR does not issue visas or give immigration advice. Full guide: <a class=\"ulink\" href=\"/golden-visa-property-ras-al-khaimah\">Golden Visa through property in Ras Al Khaimah</a>."],
];

